{"id":"b0bf19f2be812f7a348ded86ffe7dd4887d1f01a","axis":"silent","repo":"pydantic/pydantic","sha":"b0bf19f2be812f7a348ded86ffe7dd4887d1f01a","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/api/standard_library_types.md","lines":["@@ -809,6 +809,19 @@ using [`list`][] or [`tuple`][] will allow most other iterables as input, with b","     When applying [strict mode](../concepts/strict_mode.md) on collection types, strictness will *not* apply","     to the inner types. This may change in the future, see [this issue](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12319)."," ","+!!! warning \"Hash collisions with untrusted input\"","+    Building a [set](#sets) or [dictionary](#dictionaries) from crafted values can take quadratic time, as some hashes","+    (most notably for integers) aren't randomized in CPython. If the input is untrusted and this is a concern, the number","+    of items can be bounded using the `max_length` constraint:","+","+    ```python","+    from typing import Annotated","+","+    from pydantic import Field, TypeAdapter","+","+    ta = TypeAdapter(Annotated[dict[int, int], Field(max_length=100)])","+    ```","+"," ### Lists"," "," Built-in type: [`list`][] (deprecated alias: [`typing.List`][])."],"additions":13,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pydantic-core/src/validators/counter.rs","lines":["@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ use crate::input::{Input, ValidatedDict};"," use crate::tools::SchemaDict;"," "," use super::any::AnyValidator;","-use super::list::length_check;","+use super::list::{max_length_check, min_length_check};"," use super::{BuildValidator, CombinedValidator, DefinitionsBuilder, ValidationState, Validator, build_validator};"," "," #[derive(Debug)]","@@ -168,12 +168,13 @@ where"," ","             if let Some(key) = output_key {","                 output.set_item(key, output_value)?;","+                max_length_check!(self.input, \"Counter\", self.max_length, output);","             }","         }"," ","         if errors.is_empty() {","             let i